quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  2,25,"So give glad tidings to those who believe and perform righteous deeds. They shall have Gardens with rivers flowing beneath them. Whenever they are given its fruit to eat, they will say: ‘This is what we were given before,’ for they shall be given the like. In Paradise, there shall be chaste spouses for them, and they shall abide there forever."
  2,26,"Indeed, Allah is not reluctant to draw a parable, whether it is a gnat or anything more substantial than that. As for the believers, they know that it is the truth from their Lord. As for the disbelievers, they ask: ‘What could Allah mean by this parable?’ He leaves many to stray and guides many by the same. However, He leaves none to stray except the evildoers."
  2,27,"Those who break the covenant of Allah after it is confirmed, and sever (the relationship), which Allah has commanded to be joined, and cause corruption on the earth, it is they who have much to lose."
  2,28,"How do you disbelieve in Allah, (seeing that) you were lifeless and He gave you life, then He will cause you to die, and then He shall restore you to life, and then you shall be returned to Him (at last)?"
  2,29,He is the One Who created for you all that is on the earth. Then He turned to the higher regions (of the universe) and fashioned them into seven heavens. And He is All-Knowing of everything.
